1408
01:23:18,630 --> 01:23:20,910
How many times do I have to do this?

1409
01:23:20,910 --> 01:23:24,500
Is it over here?

1410
01:23:24,500 --> 01:23:25,180
*clunk*

1411
01:23:25,180 --> 01:23:26,420
*clunk*

1412
01:23:26,420 --> 01:23:27,200
*clunk*

1413
01:23:27,200 --> 01:23:27,600
Heheh~

1414
01:23:27,600 --> 01:23:33,250
Oh!

1415
01:23:33,250 --> 01:23:34,370
What's that?

1416
01:23:34,370 --> 01:23:35,230
Oh!

1417
01:23:35,230 --> 01:23:36,570
I can wash my hands?

1418
01:23:36,570 --> 01:23:40,160
No wait, what is this?

1419
01:23:40,160 --> 01:24:05,310
Huh? Now I'm confused.

1420
01:24:05,310 --> 01:24:08,160
Couldn't I wash it with this?

1421
01:24:08,160 --> 01:24:10,030
Whoa!

1422
01:24:10,030 --> 01:24:12,310
Too late now!

1423
01:24:12,310 --> 01:24:14,730
And there it goes!

1424
01:24:14,730 --> 01:24:15,130
Okay.

1425
01:24:15,130 --> 01:24:18,510
Wait, this isn't what I was reading about...

1426
01:24:18,510 --> 01:24:21,390
"Take the pork chop."

1427
01:24:21,390 --> 01:24:22,070
Which one...

1428
01:24:22,070 --> 01:24:26,360
I thought borscht was coming up next!

1429
01:24:26,360 --> 01:24:27,380
There it is, the pork chop!

1430
01:24:27,380 --> 01:24:29,200
This one...

1431
01:24:29,200 --> 01:24:34,590
Salt, pepper, thyme.

1432
01:24:34,590 --> 01:24:56,570
I think thyme was 6.

1433
01:24:56,570 --> 01:24:57,390
Isn't it black?

1434
01:24:57,390 --> 01:25:04,290
I'm not coating it evenly.

1435
01:25:04,290 --> 01:25:05,360
Hmm...

1436
01:25:05,360 --> 01:25:08,730
Aw, so close!

1437
01:25:08,730 --> 01:25:10,010
Should I wash it?

1438
01:25:10,010 --> 01:25:12,550
Will the seasoning come off if I wash it?

1439
01:25:12,550 --> 01:25:23,670
It's so black...

1440
01:25:23,670 --> 01:25:24,230
What should I do?

1441
01:25:24,230 --> 01:25:25,850
It'll be fine

1442
01:25:25,850 --> 01:25:29,680
The pot

1443
01:25:29,680 --> 01:25:31,000
30ml of sunflower oil

1444
01:25:31,000 --> 01:25:34,600
How many times, how many times—

1445
01:25:34,600 --> 01:25:44,960
What's this "mixed together" thing?

1446
01:25:44,960 --> 01:25:46,620
Maybe because I didn't wash it?

1447
01:25:46,620 --> 01:25:49,360
Uh oh, the sunflower oil is running out too

1448
01:25:49,360 --> 01:25:59,420
How many times?

1449
01:25:59,420 --> 01:26:06,610
90 minutes per side

1450
01:26:06,610 --> 01:26:08,770
90 seconds each side

1451
01:26:08,770 --> 01:26:17,380
About 1 more minute, huh

1452
01:26:17,380 --> 01:26:39,380
I shouldn't have done that

1453
01:26:39,380 --> 01:26:49,410
That's not what I was trying to do

1454
01:26:49,410 --> 01:26:53,010
I want to flip this over

1455
01:26:53,010 --> 01:27:42,920
Suddenly a baking tray

1456
01:27:42,920 --> 01:27:56,070
6g of salt

1457
01:27:56,070 --> 01:27:59,250
Is it 6g for both?

1458
01:27:59,250 --> 01:28:01,410
6g each, maybe?

1459
01:28:01,410 --> 01:28:05,430
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6

1460
01:28:05,430 --> 01:28:07,590
1, 2, 3, 4, 5

1461
01:28:07,590 --> 01:28:24,670
Aaaaaaaaaaah— dammit!

1462
01:28:24,670 --> 01:28:26,670
That was a trap, that was!

1463
01:28:26,670 --> 01:28:36,610
Make this into a 50g chunk?

1464
01:28:36,610 --> 01:28:38,330
Ah, no wait, that's wrong

1465
01:28:38,330 --> 01:28:41,290
Hmm, can't I do that here?

1466
01:28:41,290 --> 01:28:42,530
Really?

1467
01:28:42,530 --> 01:28:44,890
You can't cut on top of a baking tray

1468
01:28:44,890 --> 01:28:50,470
I want to check the gram count

1469
01:28:50,470 --> 01:28:52,570
Not salt, not salt

1470
01:28:52,570 --> 01:29:00,880
Oh!

1471
01:29:00,880 --> 01:29:03,110
Make it into a chunk?

1472
01:29:03,110 --> 01:29:04,160
Hmm?

1473
01:29:04,160 --> 01:29:06,490
Like, one by one?

1474
01:29:06,970 --> 01:29:10,210
But that doesn't mean I only need 50 total, right?

1475
01:29:10,210 --> 01:29:13,730
30, 50, 60 — if any of them are right, it should work

1476
01:29:13,730 --> 01:29:15,310
Is that no good?

1477
01:29:15,310 --> 01:29:59,870
Huh, it didn't say how many minutes... the stove

1478
01:29:59,870 --> 01:30:04,970
Let me check — oh, is it below here?

1479
01:30:04,970 --> 01:30:08,990
80

1480
01:30:08,990 --> 01:30:19,540
Oh~

1481
01:30:19,540 --> 01:30:21,460
Is this still warm?

1482
01:30:21,460 --> 01:30:22,200
It's warm

1483
01:30:22,200 --> 01:30:27,500
Hmm, but if I put this on a plate...

1484
01:30:27,500 --> 01:30:29,140
The moment I set it down

1485
01:30:29,140 --> 01:30:30,960
Like, ouch ouch ouch

1486
01:30:31,360 --> 01:30:40,790
Won't it get cold? Will it be okay?

1487
01:30:40,790 --> 01:30:45,480
Can't I do something about that — like keep it near this?

1488
01:30:45,480 --> 01:30:58,390
A little more maybe — about 1, 2, 10 more seconds, 3, 4

1489
01:30:58,390 --> 01:31:06,860
I was aiming to be a tuner from Air Gear so I'm fine — I can measure time

1490
01:31:06,860 --> 01:31:10,790
It's not fully closed

1491
01:31:10,930 --> 01:31:13,930
Okay, it's here!

1492
01:31:13,930 --> 01:31:16,950
Hot hot hot — is this even matching up right?

1493
01:31:16,950 --> 01:31:19,990
Isn't this bad?

1494
01:31:19,990 --> 01:31:22,670
I'll wash this later

1495
01:31:22,670 --> 01:31:25,090
So sorry for now

1496
01:31:25,090 --> 01:31:31,580
It is hot, for sure

1497
01:31:31,580 --> 01:31:37,880
1, 2, 3, 4, 5

1498
01:31:37,880 --> 01:31:39,850
Okay

1499
01:31:39,850 --> 01:31:43,360
Wait, is this all I need?

1500
01:31:43,360 --> 01:31:45,160
Wow, that's easy!

1501
01:31:45,160 --> 01:31:47,960
Aren't we adding any herbs today?

1502
01:31:47,960 --> 01:31:48,760
Oh, we're not?

1503
01:31:48,760 --> 01:31:49,920
Alright then

1504
01:31:49,920 --> 01:31:52,300
Come and get it~

1505
01:31:52,300 --> 01:31:53,240
Always wanted to say that

1506
01:31:53,240 --> 01:31:54,850
Yukihira...

1507
01:31:54,850 --> 01:31:55,140
Huh?

1508
01:31:55,140 --> 01:31:59,220
I hadn't tasted it

1509
01:31:59,220 --> 01:32:08,660
Huh? Wha?

1510
01:32:08,660 --> 01:32:10,360
Wait, couldn't I serve the salmon fillet?

1511
01:32:10,360 --> 01:32:11,540
Huh? Salmon fillet?

1512
01:32:11,540 --> 01:32:15,660
Salmon fillet?

1513
01:32:15,660 --> 01:32:35,150
Oh no, I gotta get ready

1514
01:32:35,150 --> 01:32:37,050
A food critic is coming

1515
01:32:37,050 --> 01:32:38,850
Isn't that soon?

1516
01:32:38,850 --> 01:32:42,270
Chicken V4 is here! This is it! I've been waiting!

1517
01:32:42,270 --> 01:32:44,950
Add to a deep plate... wait, I'm already putting it on a plate?

1518
01:32:44,950 --> 01:32:47,050
Add to a deep plate

1519
01:32:47,050 --> 01:32:48,330
Okay

1520
01:32:48,330 --> 01:32:50,890
As I command

1521
01:32:50,890 --> 01:32:54,450
Add Chicken V4.

1522
01:32:54,450 --> 01:33:03,210
Wait, so that's basically everything?

1523
01:33:03,210 --> 01:33:06,780
Can that much even fit in here?

1524
01:33:06,780 --> 01:33:10,570
There's still more to add.

1525
01:33:10,570 --> 01:33:32,610
Can I even read kanji?

1526
01:33:32,610 --> 01:33:33,950
Apparently not.

1527
01:33:33,950 --> 01:33:40,020
I'm so sorry, I'm truly, truly sorry.

1528
01:33:40,020 --> 01:33:42,500
I sincerely apologize for that.

1529
01:33:42,500 --> 01:33:47,420
Please just kill me now, I beg you.

1530
01:33:47,420 --> 01:33:48,460
Chicken V4.

1531
01:33:48,460 --> 01:33:49,520
Thanks!

1532
01:33:49,520 --> 01:33:50,940
Just kill me.

1533
01:33:50,940 --> 01:33:58,910
Oh, it's addition time!

1534
01:33:58,910 --> 01:33:59,220
With this...

1535
01:33:59,220 --> 01:33:59,820
Ah, just a sec—

1536
01:33:59,820 --> 01:34:00,280
Ah...

1537
01:34:00,280 --> 01:34:02,680
OK.

1538
01:34:02,680 --> 01:34:07,290
Salt, 20.

1539
01:34:07,290 --> 01:34:08,010
Yep.

1540
01:34:10,380 --> 01:34:15,980
Salt and pepper. Two of each.

1541
01:34:15,980 --> 01:34:21,770
Don't panic — panic means losing.

1542
01:34:21,770 --> 01:34:27,920
There we go, OK. Wait, no. Why did I add extra?

1543
01:34:27,920 --> 01:34:29,720
Hey, hey, salt!

1544
01:34:29,720 --> 01:34:32,520
OK, OK, OK, OK, OK.

1545
01:34:32,520 --> 01:34:49,900
Beets. Oh, a new one. Beets, 600.

1546
01:34:49,900 --> 01:34:51,750
Let me grab this.

1547
01:34:51,750 --> 01:34:57,110
That's a tomato.

1548
01:34:57,110 --> 01:34:58,910
That's an onion.

1549
01:34:58,910 --> 01:35:00,510
Is this the beets?

1550
01:35:00,510 --> 01:35:02,470
That's an onion!

1551
01:35:02,470 --> 01:35:04,900
Did it say 600?

1552
01:35:04,900 --> 01:35:10,820
About here should be just right.

1553
01:35:10,820 --> 01:35:12,820
Close call, close call, close call!

1554
01:35:12,820 --> 01:35:15,090
Onion, 120.

1555
01:35:15,090 --> 01:35:17,090
Carrot, 70.

1556
01:35:17,090 --> 01:35:27,060
Wait, this is a potato!

1557
01:35:27,060 --> 01:35:29,060
OK, in you go!

1558
01:35:29,060 --> 01:35:39,450
What should I do with the potato?

1559
01:35:39,450 --> 01:35:41,450
This one's probably not needed.

1560
01:35:43,250 --> 01:35:44,710
What do I do, what do I do, what do I do?

1561
01:35:44,710 --> 01:35:46,170
I'll put it around here— oh, potato!

1562
01:35:46,170 --> 01:35:47,910
Oh! Potato!

1563
01:35:47,910 --> 01:35:49,350
Alright!

1564
01:35:49,350 --> 01:35:50,530
Umm...

1565
01:35:50,530 --> 01:35:51,570
Oh! There it is! Right, I remember now!

1566
01:35:51,570 --> 01:35:53,310
There was something I needed to buy and didn't.

1567
01:35:53,310 --> 01:35:55,890
Is it flat-leaf parsley or curly parsley? Wait, no—

1568
01:35:55,890 --> 01:35:59,280
Curly parsley!

1569
01:35:59,280 --> 01:36:01,320
Oh, it's here!

1570
01:36:01,320 --> 01:36:03,260
Parsley? I had it?

1571
01:36:03,260 --> 01:36:04,460
Curly parsley!

1572
01:36:04,460 --> 01:36:10,210
A parsley-type VTuber who came from the land of parsley.

1573
01:36:10,210 --> 01:36:13,570
I... I'm parsley.

1574
01:36:13,570 --> 01:36:19,070
Found it!

1575
01:36:19,070 --> 01:36:22,130
Now, boil it!

1576
01:36:22,130 --> 01:36:26,350
Here we go!

1577
01:36:26,350 --> 01:36:29,520
Yes!

1578
01:36:29,520 --> 01:36:30,960
Today I'm going to measure properly.

1579
01:36:30,960 --> 01:36:39,700
I will absolutely measure it.

1580
01:36:39,700 --> 01:36:50,040
2 minutes?

1581
01:36:50,040 --> 01:36:53,140
Let me do some subtraction.

1582
01:36:53,140 --> 01:37:01,140
It'll be done around the 40-second mark.

1583
01:37:01,140 --> 01:37:03,780
Then the boiled mixed liquid, 300 grams.

1584
01:37:03,780 --> 01:37:05,460
Is it 300 ml from here?

1585
01:37:05,460 --> 01:37:06,500
Does it go down?

1586
01:37:06,500 --> 01:37:08,520
Whoa, amazing.

1587
01:37:08,520 --> 01:37:17,380
Prepare the deep dish.

1588
01:37:17,380 --> 01:37:19,560
Where did it go?

1589
01:37:19,560 --> 01:37:21,700
The deep dish.

1590
01:37:21,700 --> 01:37:24,200
There it is!

1591
01:37:24,200 --> 01:37:27,220
Will everything fit in here?

1592
01:37:27,220 --> 01:37:28,140
There are a lot of them though.

1593
01:37:28,140 --> 01:37:30,480
There's also one for when things break.

1594
01:37:30,480 --> 01:37:32,920
I'll put the oven dish back.

1595
01:37:32,920 --> 01:37:34,880
Hot, hot, hot!

1596
01:37:34,880 --> 01:37:36,830
Is this thing supposed to stay like this?

1597
01:37:36,830 --> 01:37:38,680
Is it actually stopped? Or is it...

1598
01:37:38,680 --> 01:37:40,480
Which one stops it?

1599
01:37:40,480 --> 01:37:42,280
Oh.

1600
01:37:42,280 --> 01:37:44,180
It finally stopped!

1601
01:37:44,180 --> 01:37:45,880
From the top?

1602
01:37:45,880 --> 01:37:47,680
Which means the one below too...

1603
01:37:47,680 --> 01:37:49,680
Wait, were you running this whole time?

1604
01:37:49,680 --> 01:37:51,480
No, it was fine.

1605
01:37:51,480 --> 01:37:59,920
Heave-ho.

1606
01:37:59,920 --> 01:38:01,920
Let me stop it for now

1607
01:38:01,920 --> 01:38:03,720
and try mixing.

1608
01:38:03,720 --> 01:38:05,520
This is it!

1609
01:38:05,520 --> 01:38:07,320
The answer I came up with,

1610
01:38:07,320 --> 01:38:08,820
the answer I settled on — this is it!

1611
01:38:08,820 --> 01:38:13,480
Huh?

1612
01:38:13,480 --> 01:38:33,190
It turned into a manual mixer.

1613
01:38:33,190 --> 01:38:42,120
300, huh...

1614
01:38:42,120 --> 01:38:44,420
That's surprisingly little?

1615
01:38:44,420 --> 01:38:59,610
I want to reduce it.

1616
01:38:59,610 --> 01:39:00,410
From here...

1617
01:39:00,410 --> 01:39:01,410
Should I scoop some out with a spoon?

1618
01:39:01,410 --> 01:39:02,010
What do I do?

1619
01:39:02,010 --> 01:39:04,110
Should I scoop some out with a spoon?

1620
01:39:04,110 --> 01:39:04,610
What do I do?

1621
01:39:04,610 --> 01:39:08,160
Maybe spill a little?

1622
01:39:08,160 --> 01:39:17,800
Oh, but maybe it's just barely...

1623
01:39:17,800 --> 01:39:18,400
Is it enough?

1624
01:39:18,400 --> 01:39:34,440
I just need to be super careful with this!

1625
01:39:35,540 --> 01:39:37,540
Having too much shouldn't be a problem, right? With this.

1626
01:39:37,540 --> 01:39:38,520
Failure.

1627
01:39:38,520 --> 01:39:40,520
Vertical, vertical, vertical.

1628
01:39:40,520 --> 01:39:47,060
Vertical.

1629
01:39:47,060 --> 01:40:24,340
It ended, it ended, it ended, didn't it.

1630
01:40:24,340 --> 01:40:33,220
I wonder if you can do this with two people or something.

1631
01:40:33,220 --> 01:40:35,020
I'd love to try that.

1632
01:40:35,020 --> 01:40:36,820
Can only one person do this? Like, just one?

1633
01:40:36,820 --> 01:40:38,420
Heave-ho.

1634
01:40:38,420 --> 01:40:40,220
I want to do this with someone who's good at cooking.

1635
01:40:40,220 --> 01:40:45,560
Please!

1636
01:40:45,560 --> 01:40:47,560
A critic who builds you up with praise, you know.

1637
01:40:47,560 --> 01:40:49,360
They were actually pretty nice. Like, genuinely.

1638
01:40:49,360 --> 01:40:51,160
Not scary at all.

1639
01:40:51,160 --> 01:40:55,160
Heave-ho.

1640
01:40:55,160 --> 01:40:55,500
Heave-ho.

1641
01:40:55,500 --> 01:41:09,660
Oh, what's this?

1642
01:41:09,660 --> 01:41:11,260
Is this the bell I got earlier?

1643
01:41:11,260 --> 01:41:14,420
I actually got a physical bell!

1644
01:41:14,420 --> 01:41:17,480
What do I do with it?

1645
01:41:17,480 --> 01:41:35,060
Do I display it?

1646
01:41:35,060 --> 01:41:40,490
I can't put it down though.

1647
01:41:40,490 --> 01:41:42,050
What is this?

1648
01:41:42,050 --> 01:41:45,250
Let me try some advanced maneuvers.

1649
01:41:45,250 --> 01:41:48,880
Let go.

1650
01:41:48,880 --> 01:41:50,380
Alright, this works!

1651
01:41:50,380 --> 01:41:58,370
Let's play test tube toss!

1652
01:41:58,370 --> 01:42:03,790
Let's wrap up today with some test tube toss.

1653
01:42:03,790 --> 01:42:09,640
Test tube toss!

1654
01:42:09,640 --> 01:42:11,920
Huh? Where do I stand for this?

1655
01:42:11,920 --> 01:42:14,160
Is here okay?

1656
01:42:14,160 --> 01:42:15,800
Is here no good?

1657
01:42:15,800 --> 01:42:18,200
If I throw from here,

1658
01:42:18,200 --> 01:42:22,900
My aim is off! It's over here!

1659
01:42:28,970 --> 01:42:31,050
No good — I need to keep a certain distance,

1660
01:42:31,050 --> 01:42:32,390
a consistent one.

1661
01:42:32,390 --> 01:42:34,950
Something like this.

1662
01:42:34,950 --> 01:42:37,110
So this is how I do it?

1663
01:42:37,110 --> 01:42:38,030
There!

1664
01:42:38,030 --> 01:42:47,980
One more, one more!

1665
01:42:47,980 --> 01:42:49,300
Another one please!

1666
01:42:49,300 --> 01:42:50,660
I wonder if a ladle would stick in it.

1667
01:42:50,660 --> 01:42:52,500
Why not?

1668
01:42:52,500 --> 01:43:00,670
It won't stick.

1669
01:43:00,670 --> 01:43:01,410
What about a fork?

1670
01:43:01,410 --> 01:43:02,970
Is the fork over there?

1671
01:43:02,970 --> 01:43:05,470
Fork please~!

1672
01:43:05,470 --> 01:43:07,830
Fork, fork!

1673
01:43:07,830 --> 01:43:09,690
Fork.

1674
01:43:09,690 --> 01:43:11,470
No fork.

1675
01:43:11,470 --> 01:43:12,650
Nope.

1676
01:43:12,650 --> 01:43:14,710
Buy one.

1677
01:43:14,710 --> 01:43:20,950
Wouldn't a skewer work for this?

1678
01:43:20,950 --> 01:43:24,840
Oh wait, there are tongs after all.

1679
01:43:24,840 --> 01:43:28,530
A knife.

1680
01:43:28,530 --> 01:43:29,570
A ping-pong knife.

1681
01:43:29,570 --> 01:43:30,770
Oh, a skewer!

1682
01:43:30,770 --> 01:43:32,670
Skewer costs 0 yen!

1683
01:43:32,670 --> 01:43:33,450
I might stab something with this

1684
01:43:33,450 --> 01:43:34,110
